/-!
# `He` satisfies the permutation-labelling criterion

The action of `He` (the TauCeti presented group) on 2058 points, given by permutation tables of
the presentation generators: the ATLAS of Group Representations permutation representation
`HeG1-p2058B0` on standard generators. The tables are checked against the relators of the TauCeti
presentation by kernel evaluation (so the representation is a homomorphism), and the representation
is faithful because the group is simple (`CFSGOutside.Corpus.fam_sporadic_converse_tauCeti`).

The point stabilizer is shown to be generated by the words `hs`: they fix the base point and a
stabilizer chain certifies that they generate a subgroup of order at least `4030387200 / 2058`, while the
corpus bound `|He| ≤ 4030387200` (`CFSGOutside.HallPaige.Corpus`) bounds the stabilizer's order from above. The
suborbit labelling is then checked to be invariant under `hs`. All certificates are checked by
kernel evaluation.
-/

namespace CFSGOutside.HallPaige.SporadicHe

